diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ad6e7a7..3d4c6e7 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -18,6 +18,28 @@ This repository contains only components specific to the desktop form factor. Co
 
 The easiest way to make changes and test Plasma Desktop during development is to [build it with kdesrc-build](https://develop.kde.org/docs/getting-started/building/).
 
+### Native NWin integration
+
+This replacement desktop uses NWin directly on Wayland: `org.kde.NWin` at
+`/NWin`, native effects interfaces, and the device manager at
+`/org/kde/NWin/InputDevice`. Device settings use
+`org.kde.NWin.InputDevice` at `/org/kde/NWin/InputDevice/<sysname>`.
+Compositor configuration is stored in `nwinrc`, and compositor shortcuts belong
+to the `nwin` component. External X11 sessions retain their separate KWin
+interfaces, `kwinrc`, shortcut component, and `_x11` virtual desktop KCM.
+
+Building requires the matching NWin SDK's `NWinDBusInterfaceConfig.cmake`
+and `NWIN_INPUTDEVICE_INTERFACE` XML definition. CMake can discover a staged
+SDK through the normal `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH`; install only into the package
+staging directory. The native workspace provides the matching
+`plasma-interactiveconsole --windowmanager` interface.
+
+Native integration entrypoints include the Mouse, Touchpad, Drawing Tablet,
+Touchscreen, Accessibility, Game Controller, Workspace Behavior, and Shortcuts
+settings, the Show Desktop, Pager, and Task Manager applets, and the
+`nwin debug console` KRunner command. Generic Plasma services, external
+KWindowSystem APIs, and published Wayland protocol names remain unchanged.
+
 ## Contributing
 
 Like other projects in the KDE ecosystem, contributions are welcome from all. This repository is managed on [KDE Invent](https://invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-desktop), our GitLab instance.
